-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",327,{
[10433]="700235B3\n1\tCollect mistletoe (total: 8)\tThe mistletoe Enit has requested can be gathered in the forest across the river to the north-west.\n2\tBring the mistletoe to Enit at Galar Culch\tEnit is at Galar Culch in the Mournshaws. You should bring the mistletoe you have collected to Enit.\n",
[10434]="700235B2\n1\tCollect oak-branches (total: 6)\tThe oak branches Enit has requested can be gathered in the northern stretches of the Mournshaws.\n2\tBring the oak branches to Enit at Galar Culch\tEnit is at Galar Culch in the Mournshaws. You should bring the oak branches you have collected to Enit.\n",
[10435]="700235B1\n1\tCollect living bark (total: 8)\tThe living bark Enit has requested can be gathered from any of the wood-trolls that stalk the forests of the Mournshaws.\n2\tBring the living bark to Enit at Galar Culch\tEnit is at Galar Culch in the Mournshaws. You should bring the living bark you have collected to Enit.\n",
[10436]="7000C0A2\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Elves of Rivendell.\n",
[10437]="7000C0A3\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Elves of Rivendell.\n",
[10438]="7000C0A4\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Elves of Rivendell.\n",
[10439]="7000C0A5\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred of the Elves of Rivendell.\n",
[10440]="7006BC45\n1\tGather Sigêma flowers (total: 4)\030Gather Bizgâr weeds (total: 4)\030Defeat Orcs near the Falls of Ilûritu (total: 6)\tEnârshan has asked you to gather Sigêma and Bizgâr as well as defeat Orcs near the Falls of Ilûritu.\n2\tReturn to Enârshan in the Falls of Ilûritu\tReturn to Enârshan with the gathered ingredients in the Falls of Ilûritu.\n",
[10441]="70060901\n1\tDefeat riverside avanc (total: 10)\tRiverside avanc can be found along the banks of the rivers in the Angle. Thalathril has asked you to dispose of the deadly avanc who plague the river-banks.\n2\tReturn to Thalathril\tThalathril is located in Tham Lumren, in the northern Angle. You should let Thalathril know that you have disposed of many riverside avanc.\n",
[10442]="700466D4\n1\tDefeat foes on the Pelennor (total: 10)\tYou should defeat any enemies you find on the after-battle Pelennor.\n2\tTalk to Éomer\tYou should talk to Éomer, who can be found at Aragorn's Pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n",
[10443]="7002D613\n1\tTalk to the master stallion in the Horse-fields\tThe master stallion is perched upon a hill overlooking the horse-farm. He has a good vantage point from which to keep an eye on his herd. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n2\tReach the first gate\tThe first gate is just to the east of the master, down the hill. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n3\tReach the second gate\tThe second gate is located east and a little south of the first gate. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n4\tReach the third gate\tThe third gate is located south-east of the second gate. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n5\tReach the fourth gate\tThe fourth gate is located south of the third gate. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n6\tReach the fifth gate\tThe fifth gate is located south-west of the fourth gate. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n7\tReach the sixth gate\tThe sixth gate is located north-west of the fifth gate. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n8\tReach the seventh gate\tThe seventh gate is located north of the sixth gate. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n9\tReach the eighth gate\tThe eighth gate is located north of the seventh gate. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n10\tReach the ninth gate\tThe ninth gate is located north-east of the eighth gate. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n11\tReturn to the master\tThe master is found overlooking the fields on his hill, just north of the ninth gate. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n12\tComplete\tThe master is found overlooking the fields on his hill, just north of the eighth gate. If defeated or time expires, you will return to Hengstacer Farm.\n",
[10444]="70022BED\n1\tFind the source of the roaring in the Cobwebbed Wing and drive it off\tSomewhere in an evil-feeling part of the Haunted Burrow, an odious roar made it clear that a bear had taken up residence in the hobbit-hole, in the Cobwebbed Wing. You should seek out the source of the roaring and drive it off so that Polo can continue his search for treasure without troublesome interruptions.\n2\tReturn to Polo Puddifoot with news of the \"bear\"\tPolo Puddifoot awaits you outside the Haunted Burrow. You should return to Polo Puddifoot and tell him of this \"bear\" you encountered.\n",
[10445]="70025BFC\n1\tDefeat tomb-robbers around Ost Forod (total: 10)\tTomb-robbers can be found in the hills north and east of Ost Forod. Clark Standish asked you to venture into the hills around Ost Forod and defeat several tomb-robbers to protect the town's winter food-supply.\n2\tTalk to Clark Standish at Ost Forod\tClark Standish is at Ost Forod. Clark Standish will be pleased to know that the tomb-robbers have several fewer mouths to feed.\n",
[10446]="70025B37\n1\tDefeat Tomb-robbers at Tham Varan (total: 6)\tTham Varan is east of Tinnudir and Tham Nambarth. Brogdagnir asked you to venture to Tham Varan and drive off the tomb robbers there.\n2\tTalk to Brogdagnir\tBrogdagnir is at Tinnudir, west of Tham Varan and Tham Nambarth. Brogdagnir will be pleased to hear the robbers will think twice before returning to Tham Varan.\n",
[10447]="70025A33\n1\tCollect Atwood's orders\030Collect Oakes' orders\tBarad Tharsír is located south-east of the colossus, in the Barandalf, on the far side of the Brandywine. Adleithian has asked you to collect orders off of two robbers, Atwood and Oakes.\n2\tBring the orders to Adleithian\tAdleithian is at the Ranger-camp at the colossus, north-west of the Barandalf and west of Parth Aduial. Adleithian is waiting to examine the orders you collected.\n",
[10448]="700266ED\n1\tDefeat tomb-robbers in Haudh Eärendur (total: 8)\tHaudh Eärendur is within the Way of Kings, west of the Ranger-camp. Nimbellas asked you to venture to Haudh Eärendur and defeat the tomb-robbers within.\n2\tTalk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings\tNimbellas is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Nimbellas will be pleased to hear that the tomb-robbers have been defeated.\n",
[10449]="700266D9\n1\tDefeat tomb-robbers at Tham Laegamon (total: 10)\tTham Laegamon is to the south-west of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Rodlam asked you to venture to Tham Laegamon and defeat the tomb-robbers there.\n2\tTalk to Rodlam\tRodlam is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Rodlam will be pleased to hear the tomb-robbers at Tham Laegamon have been defeated.\n",
[10450]="700266A3\n1\tDefeat tomb-robbers at Tham Sarch (total: 10)\tTham Sarch is in the hills south-west of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Nethrandir asked you to venture to Tham Sarch and defeat the tomb-robbers you find there.\n2\tTalk to Nethrandir\tNethrandir is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Nethrandir will be pleased to hear that the tomb-robbers have been cleared from Tham Sarch.\n",
[10451]="70072EA1\n1\tSearch for the caravan\tThe caravan is on the road ahead, to the south-east.\n2\tDefend the caravan\tThe caravan is under attack by bandits! You should defeat the bandits and defend the caravan.\n3\tDefeat Shubâza, the bandits' leader\tYou have defended the caravan by defeating the bandits and have now attracted the attention of their leader, Shubâza.\n4\tDefeat the enraged mûmak\tYou have defended the caravan by defeating the bandits as well as their leader, but now a mûmak attacks! You should defeat the enraged mûmak.\n",
[10452]="70008080\n1\tDefeat Rock-worms in Fornost (total: 5)\tWorms can be found in the ruins of Fornost, north of the Treasure Hunters' Camp. Elsie Whitman has mentioned a nagging worry about the worms to the north, and will sleep sounder if you can manage to slay some.\n2\tReturn to Elsie Whitman\tElsie Whitman is at the Treasure Hunters' Camp in the ruins of Fornost. You should return to Elsie and tell her that she may sleep easier.\n",
[10453]="7000AE1B\n1\tDeliver Rockwither's horn to Sergeant-at-Arms Caddafrith\030Collect Rockwither's horn\tRockwithers can be found in Hithlad, south of Tol Ascarnen. Sergeant-at-Arms Caddafrith has asked you to assist her in crafting a horn to call forces to fight against Angmar's army when they assail Tol Ascarnen. She needs the horn of the great aurochs Rockwithers to complete it. She suggests you take allies, for Rockwithers will be a formidable adversary.\n",
[10454]="70000758\n1\tCollect the notes and return them to Chief Watcher Grimbriar\tThe brigand leader is encamped in a copse of trees to the west of Grimbriar's post. Grimbriar awaits your return at his post at the stone house near the cross-roads of Bree. Grimbriar's spy provided information on the location of the brigand leader responsible for the latest attacks on the farms of Bree-land. Grimbriar then asked you strike a blow against the brigands and obtain any information you could from the leader.\n",
[10455]="700310EF\n1\tCross the bridge into Rohan and talk to a Rohirrim\tRohan is south of the Great River region. It is best reached by riding south from Parth Celebrant, across the Anduin by bridge. You have received a letter from Gandalf, of all people! He asks that you ride for Rohan at once.\n2\tTalk to a guard in Langhold\tThe town of Langhold is south along the road in the Wold of Rohan. You should find the town of Langhold and speak with a guard to gain admittance.\n",
[10456]="70065F82\n1\tTalk to Naremil\030Talk to Nosseth\tLothíriel has asked you to speak with Nosseth and Naremil in the Library of Saphadzîr. The Library is in Dol Amroth.\n2\tFind books on Rohan (total: 4)\tNosseth and Naremil have told you to look for books on Rohan on the second floor of the southern wing of the the Library of Saphadzîr. The Library is in Dol Amroth.\n3\tReturn to Lothíriel\tYou managed to find a few books referring to Rohan for Lothíriel. You should bring them to her in the Court of the Prince, in Dol Amroth.\n",
[10457]="7002EFBB\n1\tTag Ergrim\030Find Ergrim near the Crafting Hall\030Tag Gunmar\030Find Gunmar near the lake\030Tag Hanagild\030Find Hanagild near the stable\030Tag Béolof\030Find Béolof near the Bank\030Tag Hertsig\030Find Hertsig near the Mead Hall\tThe children are running around within Harwick. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tReturn to Garbrand\tGarbrand is in Harwick. Return to Garbrand and let him know that you played Rohirrim and Bandits with the children.\n",
[10458]="70026191\n1\tAid Lithuifin at the Even-rills\030Aid Remmenylf at the Even-rills\030Aid Erchiel at the Even-rills\tThe Elves at the Eavespires have several things to help purify the Even-rills. Longbough has asked you to work with the Elves to rid the Even-rills of the Gauredain.\n2\tTalk to Longbough at the Eavespires\tLongbough at the Eavespires. Longbough should be pleased to hear the Even-rills are now safe.\n",
[10459]="7003EB05\n1\tDefeat Stone-trolls in the Bruinen Gorges (total: 6)\tThere are Stone-trolls settled in the Bruinen Gorges of the Trollshaws, though they are rarely seen but at night. While you are in the Bruinen Gorges, you should deal with the Stone-trolls which have settled there.\n",
[10460]="700005C1\n1\tTalk to Saradoc Brandybuck at Brandy Hall\tSaradoc Brandybuck can be found at Brandy Hall at the centre of Buckland, south of the Buckland Gate. Wilmac Brandybuck has asked you to find Farmer Maggot's son Rollo. He suggested that Rollo may be off gallivanting with his friend Doderic Brandybuck, and that Doderic's uncle, Saradoc, may know where they are.\n",
[10461]="7000D3D3\n1\tTalk to Tasgall\tTasgall left Aughaire travelling north and is likely somewhere in Fasach-larran. Rona has agreed to give Crannog a favourable report of your doings if you render your aid to her brother Tasgall.\n",
[10462]="7005A99B\n1\tCollect edible mushrooms (total: 12)\tEdible mushrooms can be found at Ronglagam in Máttugard. You should collect the edible mushrooms.\n2\tPlace the edible mushrooms in a supply chest\tA supply chest can be found at any dwarf outpost in Máttugard. You should place the edible mushrooms in a supply chest.\n",
[10463]="7005A998\n1\tDestroy the stone-claw burrows\tStone-claw burrows can be found at Ronglagam in Máttugard. You should destroy the stone-claw burrows.\n2\tDestroy the stone-claw burrows (total: 10)\tStone-claw burrows can be found at Ronglagam in Máttugard. You should destroy the stone-claw burrows.\n",
[10464]="7005986E\n1\tTalk to Marigold\tHob Hayward has asked you to find Marigold Boffin before venturing into the Old Forest. You can find her just outside of Newbury, by the river's shore.\n2\tTalk to Marigold\tMarigold has offered to guide you through the forest to investigate what has been agitating the wildlife. You should let her know when you're ready to depart.\n3\tTalk to Tom Bombadil\tMarigold has taken you to see Tom Bombadil, who may know more about the situation in the forest. Tom can be found in and around his house.\n",
})
